An event has been set aside for later. Write the one line that will stand in for
it on the triage queue's backlog list.

<event kind="{{ event.kind }}" priority="{{ event.priority }}">
Received {{ event.age }}
{{ event.description }}

{{ event.payload }}
</event>

It was set aside because: {{ reason }}

Triage reads this line for exactly one purpose: to notice when something newly
arrived relates to something already set aside. So lead with the concrete
subject — who is involved, what it concerns, what is left outstanding. Someone
who has never seen the event should be able to tell from your line alone whether
an incoming message is about the same thing.

Write one line and nothing else: no preamble, no quotes, under 25 words. Do not
say that it was deferred or why, and do not editorialise about its importance;
that is not what this line is for.
